  "term": "avoidance response",
  "definition": "In cognition, an avoidance response is an immediate withdrawal-oriented reaction triggered by perceiving a threat cue, such as another person’s pain. In this source, it refers specifically to the tendency to move away from or avoid potential external danger rather than approach the injured person.",
